@startuml Scenario_1_Steady_State

title Scenario 1: Single Facility iTwin — Steady-State Operations\nMnDOT Bridge 9340 (TH-61 Corridor)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam participant {
    FontSize 11
}

actor "MicroStation /\nOpenBuildings\n(ENG)" as ENG
participant "ISBM Provider" as ISBM
actor "AssetWise\nALIM\n(REG)" as REG
actor "Maintenance\nSystem\n(MMS)" as MMS
database "Enterprise\nCIR" as CIR

note over ISBM
  **Channels for iTwin aaa-111-...**
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../maintenance/publication
  /mndot/enterprise/cir/request
end note

== Startup: Each participant opens sessions once ==

REG -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  channelUri: /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication\n  topics: ["oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry"]\n  listenerUrl: https://reg-func.azurewebsites.net/api
ISBM --> REG: sessionId: sub-reg-1

MMS -> ISBM: OpenSubscriptionSession\n  channelUri: /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication\n  topics: ["oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry"]\n  listenerUrl: https://mms-func.azurewebsites.net/api
ISBM --> MMS: sessionId: sub-mms-1

ENG -> ISBM: OpenPublicationSession\n  channelUri: /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication
ISBM --> ENG: sessionId: pub-eng-1

REG -> ISBM: OpenPublicationSession\n  channelUri: /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication
ISBM --> REG: sessionId: pub-reg-1

== Operational Flow: Tag Update Propagates Through the Chain ==

ENG -> ISBM: PostPublication\n  topic: oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry\n  body: <ProcessRegistry>\n    TIC-106 installed on Bridge 9340\n  </ProcessRegistry>
ISBM --> ENG: messageId: msg-001

ISBM -> REG: PUT /notifications/sub-reg-1/msg-001\n  { topics: ["oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry"] }
activate REG

REG -> ISBM: ReadPublication (sub-reg-1)
ISBM --> REG: ProcessRegistry BOD (TIC-106)

REG -> REG: Map TIC-106 → LOC-000001\n(functional location)

REG -> ISBM: OpenConsumerRequestSession\n  channelUri: /mndot/enterprise/cir/request
ISBM --> REG: sessionId: cons-reg-1

REG -> ISBM: PostRequest (cons-reg-1)\n  ProcessRegistry: TIC-106 ↔ LOC-000001
ISBM --> REG: requestMsgId: req-001

note over CIR: CIR receives request via\nits own provider session\non /mndot/enterprise/cir/request

CIR -> ISBM: PostResponse\n  AcknowledgeRegistry\n  CIRID: CIR-00042
ISBM --> CIR: messageId: resp-001

REG -> ISBM: ReadResponse (cons-reg-1, req-001)
ISBM --> REG: AcknowledgeRegistry (CIRID: CIR-00042)

REG -> ISBM: RemovePublication (sub-reg-1)
REG -> ISBM: PostPublication (pub-reg-1)\n  topic: oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry\n  body: LOC-000001 with CIRID
ISBM --> REG: messageId: msg-002
deactivate REG

ISBM -> MMS: PUT /notifications/sub-mms-1/msg-002\n  { topics: ["oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry"] }
activate MMS

MMS -> ISBM: ReadPublication (sub-mms-1)
ISBM --> MMS: ProcessRegistry BOD (LOC-000001, CIRID: CIR-00042)

MMS -> MMS: Map LOC-000001 → 234441\n(maintenance asset ID)

MMS -> ISBM: RemovePublication (sub-mms-1)
deactivate MMS

note over ENG, MMS
  **Result: Three systems, one physical asset**
  ENG: TIC-106 (engineering tag)
  REG: LOC-000001 (functional location)
  MMS: 234441 (maintenance asset)
  CIR: All three linked under CIRID CIR-00042
end note

@enduml
